# Local to services/evidence, deliberately NOT added to the repo-root .gitignore.
#
# The root file's `/target/` rule is anchored (leading slash) because an earlier
# unanchored `target/` silently dropped apps/ares-sec/src/target/ from an import.
# That rule carries an incident and is not worth reopening, and a per-directory
# .gitignore is already the house pattern here (core/, apps/*, supabase/ all have
# their own).

# Rust build output for the two independent cargo workspaces under onchain/.
onchain/spec/target/
onchain/anchor/target/

# Anchor CLI scratch. Only appears once someone installs the Solana toolchain;
# listed now so the first person to run `anchor build` does not commit it.
onchain/anchor/.anchor/
onchain/anchor/test-ledger/

# Keypairs. A program keypair is a private key: it is generated by an operator,
# never by CI and never by an agent. Belt-and-braces, because committing one
# would hand over the program's upgrade authority.
**/*-keypair.json

# Bundles produced by a local run. The committed ones live in vectors/ and are
# named explicitly, so a stray bundle beside a scratch report never lands.
*.evidence.json
!vectors/*.evidence.json
